# Token economy (K-Pax)

Quality and correctness beat saving tokens. Never invent code you have not verified. Save tokens by **narrow context**, not by skipping needed reads.

## Two stages

1. **Find** — Grep/Glob under one area (`lib/`, `server/`, `windows/`, …). Prefer `.cursor/project-source-index.txt` + `AGENTS.md` over listing the repo.
2. **Read** — Only matched files; use offset/limit on large files. Then edit.

Skip stage 1 when the user already gave an exact path.

## Hard limits

- Do not re-read a file unchanged in this chat; reuse what you already have.
- Do not open `third_party/`, `build/`, `.dart_tool/`, or full platform trees unless the task is there.
- Shell/test output: summarize; do not paste walls of logs into the next step. Cap follow-up reads of logs at ~100 lines of signal.
- No workspace-wide ripgrep with vague patterns. Narrow path + symbol/string first.
- If after one focused search the locus is unclear — ask (client / server / ios / windows) instead of scanning everything.

## Still required

- Read enough to match existing patterns before changing code.
- After edits, check lints on touched files when tools allow.
- Do not weaken security, networking, or payment paths to “save tokens”.
